      "side": 1,
      "message": "Checked on the largest system I have on hand: 37 FRUs (busctl tree | grep -c FruDevice) on a 1 GB BMC.\n\nThe cache stores raw FRU bytes per (bus,address); maxFruSize caps a single FRU at 512 bytes. Worst case here is 37 * (512 + ~64) ≈ ~21 KB, and typical FRUs (~256 bytes) are about half that.\n\nEven an order of magnitude more FRUs would only be ~200 KB, so I don\u0027t think it\u0027s a concern on any realistic config.\n\nIt\u0027s also not really new memory pressure: fru-device already holds every FRU\u0027s bytes in busmap (DeviceMap) during a scan, so publishedFru is a second copy of the same data — same order of magnitude as what\u0027s already kept, not a multiple of it.",
      "parentUuid": "b8bb4ab1_161230b6",
      "revId": "e00a7eba8307fa0a1634adeedda0f436c1f86a49",
